          %p
            In (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"}> enriched
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            by a
            %em cosmos
            one means a “good place in which to do (enriched) category theory”. Typically what is meant is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+of+enrichment"} base of enrichment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            (being by default a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            or more generally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            or similar) which carries enough extra structure for intended
            = succeed "-constructions" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category-theoretic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+categories"} enriched functor categories
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
          %p
            The word is chosen by analogy with the notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/toposes"} toposes
            which may be regarded as “a good places to do
